---
title: Cheesy Taco Pasta
servings: 6
prepTime: 5 mins
cookTime: 20 mins
source: https://emilybites.com/2011/11/cheesy-taco-pasta.html
tags: Beef
---

Cook @pasta shells{8%oz} according to package instructions.

While pasta is cooking, cook @ground beef{1%lb}(95% lean) in a #large skillet{}
over medium-high heat, breaking up the beef as it cooks.
When the beef is cooked, drain any grease from pan.

Add the @taco seasoning{1%oz}(packet), @salsa{1.5%cups}(chunky), and @water{1/2%cup} and reduce heat to simmer.
Simmer for ~{5%minutes} or until pasta is done cooking.

Once pasta is done, drain pasta and add it to the beef mixture.
Add the @sour cream{1/4cup}, @cheddar cheese{3/4%cup}(shredded), @sharp cheddar cheese{3/4%cup}(shredded),
@salt, and @pepper and stir to combine.
Cheese will melt when thoroughly mixed.

Remove from heat and serve immediately.

= Nutritional Information (per serving) =
376 calories, 37 g carbs, 5 g sugars, 13 g fat, 6 g saturated fat, 29 g protein, 6 g fiber
